---
description: Rules for the durable-flow project
alwaysApply: true
---
- Read docs/ (or the master spec) before changing engine logic.
- internal/ is the engine. examples/ and cmd/demo-* import sdk/ only, never internal/.
- Hand-written SQL with pgx. No ORM.
- Every state transition for a workflow runs in one transaction that first does
  SELECT ... FOR UPDATE on the workflows row.
- Any task completion/heartbeat/failure must verify status='leased' AND lease_token matches.
- Workflow code must stay deterministic: no time.Now, rand, uuid, goroutines, map-order dependence.
- Never change a test to make it pass. If a test fails, explain why and fix the code,
  or ask me if the test itself is wrong.
- Do not add dependencies without asking.
- Keep functions small, return errors with context (fmt.Errorf("...: %w", err)).
- Before writing code for a phase marked HARD, explain the design in plain
  English, list the failure cases, and wait for my confirmation.
